# Injection Hygiene & Consumables Protocol

> [!abstract] Owns injection logistics and consumables.
> Product owners include [[Alcohol Swab (100pcs) — Shopee]], [[Insulin Syringe 30g (NIPRO) (100pcs) — Shopee]], and [[Insulin Syringe 31g (100pcs) — Local Pharmacy]]. This protocol also owns clean prep, vial dating, needle/syringe disposal, and consumable stock forecasting for peptides, HCG/HMG, insulin-risk products, and other injectables.

> [!danger] Boundary
> This is safety infrastructure, not training to self-administer prescription or research injectables. Technique, route, dose, sterile compounding, and reconstitution should be clinician/pharmacist taught. If sterility is questionable, discard.

## Operating Rule

One injection event requires a complete sterile workflow. If any part is missing, the injection is delayed rather than improvised.

Minimum rule set:

- New sterile syringe and needle every time.
- Alcohol swab for vial top and skin when appropriate.
- Clean prep surface away from sinks, food, pets, and clutter.
- No needle left sitting in a vial septum.
- No reuse, sharing, backloading from dirty surfaces, or saving questionable leftovers.
- Sharps go directly into a puncture-resistant sharps container.

